org.gov2.ro: public institutions of Romania
This file lists the sources of the data and their terms. It is not legal advice.

Our own contribution (selection, matching, families, categories, curation files) is offered under EUPL v1.2.
This licence does not cover the source data. Each source keeps its own terms, below.
Where two texts of one source disagree, we apply the strictest text and name both.
This project is not an official project of the Government of Romania. No publisher approves it.
The same data is in metadata.json (keys "sources" and "licence_note").

1. Lista entităților publice. Ministerul Finanțelor (ANAF), data.gov.ro. Copy of 2026-10-01.
   Licence: OGL-ROU-1.0 (https://data.gov.ro/base/images/logoinst/OGL-ROU-1.0.pdf).
   An older ANAF notice allows reproduction with the source named.
   Conține informații publice în baza Licenței pentru Guvernare Deschisă v1.0.
   Changes: records matched, categorised and linked to other sources.
2. Achiziții publice (SEAP). Autoritatea pentru Digitalizarea României, data.gov.ro. Copy of 2026-11-03.
   Licence: CC BY 4.0 (2021-2026) and OGL-ROU-1.0 (older sets).
   Changes: authority name, CUI, years, type and locality only; rows merged by CUI.
3. Date de identificare plătitori. Ministerul Finanțelor, data.gov.ro. Snapshot of 2026-06-11 (set updated July 2026). CC BY 4.0.
   Changes: status label mapped to our values; county filled where empty. Natural persons skipped.
4. Firme înregistrate la Registrul Comerțului până la data de 19.10.2026. ONRC, data.gov.ro. CC BY 4.0.
   Changes: the CUI of some records only.
5. ROePAS (Autoritatea pentru Digitalizarea României). Copy of 2026-10-05.
   Terms: no mass copying, no scraping, consent needed. Consent is not on record.
   Status: open question for the owner. See docs/reports/source-licences.md.
6. Registrul Național al Instituțiilor Publice din România (PDF of 2020, e-guvernare.ro). No licence found. Publisher not proved.
7. Declarații de integritate (ANI), aggregate counts through monitorul.ai. Copy of 2026-10-19.
   Reproduction with the source. No written terms of access.
8. posturi.gov.ro (Guvernul României). Terms not readable on 2026-11-05 and 2026-11-23.
9. Maps: geo-spatial.org, from data of ANCPI. Version 2025-03-26.
   The page footer of geo-spatial.org states CC BY-SA 4.0. The catalogue record (edition 2025-05-05) states CC BY 4.0.
   We apply the stricter text. The map files are under CC BY-SA 4.0, not under EUPL.
   Changed: split by county, simplified, SIRUTA codes and labels added.
10. Fonts: Inter and Fragment Mono, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (notices in assets/gov2/fonts/).
11. County coats of arms (explorer/assets/steme-judete/, table SOURCES.csv, checked on 2026-11-23 on Wikimedia Commons).
    Our PNG files are resized copies. We found the Commons file of 12 of the 42 files by comparing the pictures:
    AG, B, BH, BZ, HD, MH, MS, NT, OT, SB, SJ, VN. All 12 are marked "Public domain" on Commons.
    The author named on Commons is in SOURCES.csv (mostly the county councils). No attribution is required.
    The origin of the other 30 files is not proved. For each, SOURCES.csv names the Commons file
    that the Romanian Wikipedia shows in the county article. Our file is not shown to be that drawing.
    The Commons files of these counties are marked "Public domain" or CC0. This does not prove the licence of our files.
    The coat of arms of a public authority is an official symbol (Legea 8/1996, art. 9; not verified by the project).
    A specific drawing can still have an author.
12. Link only, no other data taken: tipizatul.eu (we keep their spelling of 448 institution names to build the link).
13. Transparenta.eu (entity list, parent CUIs, date of the latest report; no profile data). Copy of 2026-11-23.
    The data comes from the ANAF budget execution reports, so OGL-ROU-1.0 applies (https://data.gov.ro/base/images/logoinst/OGL-ROU-1.0.pdf).
    The terms of Transparenta.eu say that open data follows the licence of its source. Source: ANAF, via Transparenta.eu.
    Changes: some records and parents added by a rule. The name, address and county of a new record come from Transparenta.eu.
    A lookup in the ANAF PlatitorTvaRest service only confirms that a new record is active; no field of that service is published.
